<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4020.12">
  <POU Name="F_AxisRef_To_MSTA" Id="{6037187c-3053-436d-ba08-ac7db25710cf}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(* F_AxisRef_To_MSTA - axis status to EPICS pseudo-MSTA word

Purpose:
    Translate one manipulator axis (ST_ManipAxis, owned and updated by
    FB_ManipAxis) into the UINT status word that is exposed to EPICS as the
    axis MSTA. Only the MSTA bits this project actually reports are assigned;
    the remaining bits carry no meaning.

Usage:
    Call once per PLC cycle, after the matching FB_ManipAxis instance has run:
        F_AxisRef_To_MSTA(stManipAxis := iq_Injector.axisX,
                          MSTA         => iq_Injector.axisX.uiMsta);
    The function is stateless and does not modify stManipAxis, so it can be
    called for as many axes as needed, in any order.

Objectives:
    - Keep the ST_ManipAxis to MSTA bit mapping in exactly one place instead of
      repeating bit twiddling in every consumer of the axis status.
    - Make the bit contract of MSTA readable from this POU interface alone, so
      consumers do not have to reverse-engineer the meaning of the word.

MSTA bit layout (dimensionless bit field, no engineering units):
    bit 0    axis enabled   TRUE while the axis is powered/enabled
                           (stManipAxis.xEnabled)
    bit 1    axis error     TRUE while the axis reports an error
                           (stManipAxis.stAxis.Status.Error)
    bits 2-15              not assigned by this function; do not rely on them
    Test the individual bits (MSTA.0 enabled, MSTA.1 error) rather than the
    whole word.

History:
    17/8/17    - A. Wallace - Created: translates the axis ref status to an
                               EPICS pseudo MSTA value.
    2026-11-28 - Documentation only: added this POU header and the
                 declaration comments (bit mapping unchanged).
*)
FUNCTION F_AxisRef_To_MSTA	: UINT
VAR_INPUT
    stManipAxis	:	ST_ManipAxis; (* Axis status/control struct to translate, as owned
                                     by FB_ManipAxis. Supplies bit 0 of MSTA via
                                     xEnabled and bit 1 via stAxis.Status.Error; read
                                     only, never modified by this function. *)
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    MSTA	:	UINT; (* EPICS pseudo MSTA status word of the axis, a dimensionless
                       bit field: bit 0 = axis enabled, bit 1 = axis error, all
                       other bits unused. *)
END_VAR
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[(* This block translates the axis ref status to an EPICS psuedo MSTA value *)
(* A. Wallace, 17/8/17 *)

MSTA.1 := stManipAxis.stAxis.Status.Error;
MSTA.0 := stManipAxis.xEnabled;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>